            "new_string": "### 51.1 Token telemetry: per-request LLM cost accounting\n- [ ] Build request-level cost profiling so token usage is measurable,\n      not guessed.  Two goals: (a) make token cost visible, (b) minimize\n      cases that need model judgment.\n  - Record per-call: input char/token count, whether LLM was triggered,\n    how many LLM round-trips, prompt/completion tokens per round-trip,\n    rule hit count, ambiguous term count, final fix count, profile,\n    content_type.\n  - Derive three core metrics:\n    1. Average token cost per 1000 chars.\n    2. LLM token share of total per-call cost.\n    3. Average tokens spent per ambiguous term.\n  - Output: structured JSON block appended to tool response when\n    `include_telemetry: true` (MCP) or `--telemetry` (CLI).  Zero\n    overhead when disabled.\n  - Prerequisite: 44.1 (tracing) provides the span infrastructure;\n    51.1 adds token-specific counters on top.\n  - Scope: `src/mcp/sampling.rs` (token counters), `src/mcp/tools.rs`\n    (aggregation + output), `src/main.rs` (CLI flag).\n  - Gate: `--telemetry` on a file with 2 ambiguous terms shows\n    per-term token breakdown.  Zero-ambiguity files show LLM=0.\n\n### 44.2 CPU profiling infrastructure for scan pipeline ✅",
